 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "52 and 54 (Hell, the ransom): nothing drawn, no gold motif. 53 is the Prophet's ﷺ answer: no plate. The deniers' question is framed by As-Sa'di («على وجه التعنت والعناد»). Stars for the heavens (55:5-7), geometric for the promise of Allah (55:10-12), night and day for giving life and death (56:2-3). STAGING v4: Stays ambient throughout (no this-world scene to stage): 52 is the Hereafter (the punishment of eternity), 53 is the deniers asking the Prophet ﷺ and his sworn answer (how people behave toward him is never staged: a group asking toward an empty side would stand for him), 54 is the Day (the ransom, the hidden regret, the judgement), 55-56 are Allah's dominion, His promise and His giving life and death. c2: no plate at all (camera and the geometric background only) and params.quiet over 53:1-8, the address to the Prophet ﷺ and his sworn answer. c3 (55-56): mood changed from light to geometric, as 55:10-12 includes the promise of punishment for the polytheists (Al-Muyassar) and 56:4-5 the return for recompense (As-Sa'di); light is never the mood over a threat. No scales at the judgement (54:16-18), no gold for the ransom (54:6-10)."
